Working on PC 1 (Making Changes)
 When you are done writing code on your first computer, send it to GitHub:Press Ctrl + K (or Cmd + K on Mac) to open the Commit screen.
 Check the boxes next to your changed files and type a short message.
 Hover over the Commit button, click the small arrow next to it, and choose Commit and Push.
 Click Push on the next screen. Your code is now safely on GitHub.

Switching to PC 2 (Getting Changes)
 Before you type even a single line of new code on your second computer,
 pull the latest updates down:Open IntelliJ on your second computer.
 Press Ctrl + T (or Cmd + T on Mac) to update the project.Click OK on the small window that pops up.
 Your second computer will instantly update with the files you edited on PC 1.